<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Wars of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lithuanian Wars of Freedom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian Wars of Independence were the three wars that newly independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> fought after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>: against Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-russian-volunteer-army">West Russian Volunteer Army</a>, known as the Bermontians, and against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Lithuania defeated the Soviet and Bermontian forces in 1919, but Poland kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> after Żeligowski's mutiny of 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-wars-of-independence.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Wars of Independence" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volunteers_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_heading_to_the_Lithuanian_Wars_of_Independence_in_Vilkavi%C5%A1kis,_1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
